let's talk about a really fascinating  blockchain project called seek Cee K  seek is looking to combine virtual  reality with blockchain and primarily  this would be for the consumption of  live events so concerts for example  through the use of VR their token sale  is over &amp; Seek tokens are already on  major crypto exchanges and right now  what they're getting ready for is the  launch of their first blockchain so to  begin with let's talk a little bit about  the background of the problem that seek  is trying to solve every year 60 million  concert tickets are sold in the US but  it could be a much higher number and  market research shows that demand for  live music events is higher than ever  and musical artists aren't able to meet  all of the demand because artists can  only perform a certain number of  concerts a year a month a week whatever  so they end up having to turn down lots  of people who want to attend and this  also means lost revenue for the artists  and it means that fans are missing out  maybe your favorite artist isn't coming  to your town or the concert that there  is nearby is sold out and seek solution  is to almost infinitely extend the reach  of concerts through the people who want  to use virtual reality to see those  concerts and they're already doing this  seek is a VR company that has been  around for a little while  even before they started tokenizing  their platform they produce a patented  VR headset which can already be bought  at a bunch of different retailers and  they develop VR software including an  app for Android and for iOS which you  can use with other VR headsets not just  the one that they make and they also do  VR content you're already able to use  that app to watch concerts in virtual  reality people like Elton John Katy  Perry lady get Lady Gaga even Megadeth  is part of the platform and actually one  of seeks projects with Megadeth won a  Grammy Award  they've got partnership deals with  Universal Music Group with Apple with  t-mobile so it's a well-established  platform especially compared to some of  the other platforms that have been  tokenizing over the last months or even  year or two  what they're  now doing is building a blockchain  ecosystem on top of the platform that  they already have because they say that  this is going to make for a more user  friendly experience where you're not  having to take off your headset and  leave the VR world to get out your  credit card for example and you can have  that virtual reality experience  uninterrupted seek also is thinking  about this move to tokens from the  transparency perspective at the  transactional level right everything  will be crypto based so it's all  trackable music artists the record  labels the fans everybody knows really  where the money is going and for what  reason under what pretense money is  moving so here's how it works  seek has a mechanism within their  blockchain platform called the celebrity  coin mint artists and music labels use  the celebrity coin Mint to create custom  coins that serve like a ticket to an  event and fans then use those coins for  admission to live VR concerts or VIP  events the meet and greets any kind of  event that a music artist might want to  put on and the celebrity coin mint will  also allow artists and labels to create  virtual merchandise like for example  custom skins that you can use within the  virtual universe of seek other  collectible virtual goods that brands  and music artists might want to  distribute to their fans pretty  limitless possibilities there the idea  is that music artists will only release  a small number of each item so that the  items are rare and could even go up in  value on the market that exists within  the siik platform and each of these  items will have their own aetherium  address on the siik blockchain so each  item is actually unique and certified  authentic which is another reason that  Sikh also wants to tokenize music  artists will even be able to  cryptographically autographed digital  items in the virtual world in a way that  can't be duplicated which also has the  possibility of making those items more  valuable and all of these coins which  against  service tickets for events as well as  for the virtual merchandise it will all  function like crypto within the platform  and people can buy and sell them in VR  like cryptocurrency because again they  all will have unique aetherium addresses  basically everything within what they  call the seek VR environment  entertainment Metaverse is powered by  this blockchain and it's also powered by  the token the seek token is what you use  to buy and sell all of these things that  we're talking about you can actually buy  the seek VR headsets using the tokens  users can also earn seek tokens by  creating lists of music artists that  they want to see perform in VR concerts  which helps the platform figure out  which artists are most in demand you can  also earn seek tokens by sharing a  unique tracking URL on your social media  in order to grow the Sikh community and  they also want to branch out to content  beyond music events I actually spoke to  the CEO and she explained that this  could really be used for anything right  sporting events they already have  partnerships with a few NBA teams yoga  classes medical training taking a  foreign language class anything we're  actually feeling like you're there in  person is important could be used within  the Sikh metaphors so all types of  content creators whether you're a math  tutor or a Grammy Award winning musical  artist you can earn seek tokens by  providing content to the platform  developers developers can earn tokens by  designing those virtual merch items that  I was talking about and by designing  virtual environments within the virtual  world of siik which they call Sikh City  it's kind of like a virtual portal to  all of that VR content and you can earn  tokens by playing an administrative role  within that Sikh city Mary spy o is the  CEO  she holds ten technology patents she's  the former head of satellite  communications at Bo  and is on the advisory board of oculus  VR we interviewed her recently super  interesting interview  Christopher Cramer is a blockchain  engineer cloud computing expert has won  the IBM global entrepreneurs award and  then Laurie Clark is the chief operating  officer a graduate of Harvard Business  School and a former senior VP at Staples  so the big picture here is that seek  offers their own VR headset hardware  that you can buy they're also solving a  huge problem that exists in the VR  industry by offering a platform and  content that can be accessed by an array  of different types of VR headsets and  the problem that I find concerning  within the VR industry is the  fragmentation that exists tons of VR  companies are selling proprietary  hardware here you can buy the headset or  you can use a different headset in many  circumstances you buy a headset you can  only access content designed for that  headset and that stifles everybody  that's titles developers that stifles  the hardware manufacturers seek is  allowing people to access their  ecosystem regardless of which hardware  you are using which I believe will be  productive characteristic for their  progress in the industry but what I see  as most central to the project is how  they are facilitating a solution to two  major problems in the entertainment  industry number one miss revenue  opportunities for performers and  educators I know a ton of these  performers and educators who believe me  folks are missing revenue opportunities  and then also there are consumers that  are missing opportunities to consume  live events whether it's because you  can't afford or get a ticket to a  concert that might be a couple of states  away or on the other side of the planet  or because there's trainings that you'd  like to go to but it's just not  convenient given your work schedule a  lot of consumers will benefit from  having access to these events and it  really could shake up the VR industry if  seek is successful in what they're  trying to accomplish and they're off to  a really great start I encourage you to  check out seek using the link under this  video and of course none of what I've  said is a  financial endorsement or financial  advice of any kind I'm talking about  project this is a tokenized blockchain  crypto project everybody should do their  own due diligence the way that I do and  the way that I advocate that everybody  always do before making any financial  decision

